             'subscription. |'),
        ),
        '## MQTT Transport Binding > ### Layer 1 evidence families': (
            ('The topic carries exactly five families, discriminated by the **single top-level key '
             'beside `signature`**:'),
            ('| Key | Family | Inner grammar owned by |'),
            ('| `envelope` | Telemetry, heartbeats included | This contract |'),
            ('| `fault` | Fault events | This contract |'),
            ('| `maintenance_event` | Maintenance lifecycle events | This contract |'),
            ('| `result` | Device-configuration results | '
             '[device-configuration/v1.md](../device-configuration/v1.md) |'),
            ('| `command_result` | Firmware command results | '
             '[firmware-command-result/v1.md](../firmware-command-result/v1.md) |'),
            ('The list is closed.'),
            ('A payload carrying any other top-level key, more than one of these keys, or a key it '
             'cannot match exactly is rejected — never routed by guesswork, and never inspected '
             'further to infer what it might have meant.'),
            ('Discrimination is on the key alone, before the inner object is read, so a '
             'receiver never'
             ' has to decide a family from fields it has not yet verified.'),
            ('All five consume `seq` from **one** `(boot_id, seq)` stream and are checked against '
             '**one** high-water mark.'),
            ('There is no per-family freshness state.'),
            ('A receiver that kept separate marks would accept a replayed envelope of one '
             'family while'
             ' its neighbour advanced, which is the failure the single stream exists to prevent.'),
            ('Every payload, whichever family, MUST pass the same verification before a '
             'receiver acts '
             'on it: provisioning-anchor eligibility, the pinned manifest, envelope signature, '
             '`(boot_id, seq)` freshness against the shared high-water mark, `posture` '
             'agreement, and '
             'canonical shape.'),
            ('The same offline-buffering obligations apply to all five.'),
            ('A payload carries exactly one family key.'),
            ('A consumer refuses one that carries two or more, and never routes it by the first '
             'key it'
             ' tests.'),
            ('A consumer that has not adopted a family does not consume it: it acts on nothing the '
             'payload says, and this version does not require it to record a refusal.'),
            ('No family other than `envelope` establishes, extends or restores runtime '
             'supervision, '
             'liveness or reachability, so a device cannot hold a backstop suppressed by '
             'publishing '
             'faults, events or results.'),
            ('A receiver MUST NOT relax any of these because a family describes intended '
             'operations '
             'rather than faults.'),
            ('An unverified maintenance event is exactly the message an attacker would forge to '
             'explain away a suppressed interlock, and an unverified configuration result is '
             'exactly '
             'the message they would forge to convince a provisioner that a limit it never set '
             'is in '
             'force.'),
        ),
        '## Signed Fault Events': (
            ("v1's description of a fault event reads, in this version:"),
            ("A fault event is device-signed evidence about the device's own conduct: what it "
             'refused, what it protected against, and where it could not keep a guarantee it is '
             'supposed to keep.'),
            ('A rejected command, corrupt sensor input suspending a local interlock, an '
             'interlock trip, a brownout-path failure, a sensor that stopped answering, '
             'evidence the device could not make durable.'),
            ('The common property is that the device is reporting on itself, not on the world '
             'it measures.'),
            ("It shares the telemetry envelope's identity and freshness fields, consumes `seq` "
             'from the same counter (one monotonic stream per key epoch — one replay state), '
             'and follows the same canonical JSON and signature rules.'),
            ("v1's sentence on what a fault event is for reads, in this version:"),
            ('A fault event must never be converted into a `SensorReading` and must never '
             "trigger actions; it is evidence about the device's own conduct — what it refused, "
             'what it protected, and where it could not keep its own guarantees.'),
            ("A fault object is v1's, field for field, except for `v`:"),
            ('| Field | Type | Notes |'),
            ("| `v` | `int` | The fault object's version:"),
            ('`1` or `2`.'),
            ("Unlike v1, it is not the telemetry envelope's `v`, which is `1` or `2` "
             'independently of it. |'),
        ),
        '## Signed Fault Events > ### Fault Fields': (
            ("v1's `subject` and `detail` rows read, in this version:"),
            ('| Field | Type | Notes |'),
            ('| `subject` | `string` | The channel, rule, or action the fault concerns, from '
             'the fleet identifier alphabet.'),
            ('May be empty when no subject applies.'),
            ('At most 63 characters. |'),
            ('| `detail` | `string` | A short machine-readable token qualifying the code (for '
             '`command_rejected`, the command verdict exactly as named in '
             '`firmware-commands/v1.md`; for interlock faults, the rule name).'),
            ('May be empty.'),
            ('At most 63 characters. |'),
            ('`subject` and `detail` are bounded at **63 characters** and restricted to the '
             'fleet identifier alphabet (`A-Z`, `a-z`, `0-9`, `.`, `_`, `-`).'),
            ('The bound is normative on both sides: producers cannot emit a longer token, and '
             'consumers MUST reject a fault carrying one even when its signature verifies.'),
            ('A valid signature over an unrepresentable shape means the two implementations '
             'disagree about the contract, which is exactly what the shared fault vectors exist '
