            ('[ori-specs#49](https://github.com/ori-platform/ori-specs/issues/49) tracks the '
             'one that will.'),
            ('A consumer therefore MUST NOT infer from the absence of a completion event that a '
             'window is still active; absence means the outcome was not durably recorded, not '
             'that suppression continues.'),
            ('Neither recovery event asserts anything about how the previous window ended.'),
            ('That outcome was lost with the write that failed, and no later event can recover '
             'it.'),
            ('In particular **there is no event asserting that a reboot interrupted '
