        '## Late Faults': (
            ("A fault's `boot_id`, `seq` and `device_uptime_ms` are those of the moment it is "
             'signed.'),
            ('A producer that reports a condition late signs each report with the freshness '
             'fields of its own reporting, never with those of the condition.'),
            ('That covers a report made from a latch, a report made on a later boot, and every '
             'retry of a report the producer could not make durable: each attempt is stamped '
             'when it is signed.'),
            ('A consumer cannot tell a late report from a prompt one, so these rules attach to '
             'the code, whenever the fault was signed.'),
            ("They do not touch verification: a fault's freshness fields are still checked "
             'exactly as v1 checks them, and they still establish that the report itself is '
             'fresh.'),
            ('What they cannot establish is when the condition occurred, or anything about '
             "authority or the device's current state."),
            ('For a fault whose code is `storage_degraded`, `brownout_relay_fault`, '
             '`sensor_fault` or `ingress_degraded`:'),
            ('A consumer MUST NOT use its freshness fields to locate the condition, to derive '
             'how long it lasted, or to derive any authority.'),
            ('The fault asserts that the condition occurred on the device, not when, and not '
             'that it still held when the fault was signed.'),
            ('A consumer MAY count the reports it accepted, named as reports, and MUST NOT '
             'present or use that number as a count of failures, outages or affected commands.'),
            ('One condition can be reported more than once: a producer that made a report '
             'durable but could not then clear the latch that owed it reports it again, on the '
             'same boot or a later one.'),
            ('Several conditions can also be coalesced into one report.'),
            ('A consumer MUST NOT treat the absence of such a fault as evidence that the '
             'condition did not occur.'),
            ('[`storage_degraded` Is Late and Incomplete by '
             'Construction](#storage_degraded-is-late-and-incomplete-by-construction) says this '
