        '## Reading Envelope at `v` 2 > ### Producers': (
            ('A producer that implements this section signs every envelope at `v` `2`, readings '
             'and heartbeats alike, and always includes `liveness_nonce`, `null` when it holds no '
             'nonce.'),
            ('Envelopes it signed before it implemented this section and still holds in its '
             'offline buffer are retransmitted unchanged, at `v` `1`: retransmission is not '
             'signing.'),
            ('**A reading carries the nonce held when its measurement began.** The producer '
             'captures the held nonce before the first bus or sensor operation of the first '
             'transaction the envelope represents, and carries that value unchanged through '
             'validation, sequence reservation, signing and buffering.'),
            ("A liveness message accepted after that point is not the envelope's nonce."),
            ('That includes one accepted while a fault owed from an earlier condition is '
             'published, or while the buffer is flushed, between the read and the signing.'),
            ('**Every reading in an envelope comes from a transaction begun after its nonce was '
             'accepted.** A producer MUST NOT sign a nonce beside a reading whose transaction '
             'began before that nonce was accepted.'),
            ('An envelope that includes a cached reading, or readings collected independently, '
             'carries a nonce accepted before every one of their transactions began, and '
             'otherwise `null`.'),
            ('An alarm-word reading is still signed alone in its envelope, as [Controller '
             'Profiles](#controller-profiles) requires.'),
            ('**A heartbeat carries the nonce held when it is signed.** A heartbeat measures '
             'nothing.'),
            ('**A fault carries none.** The fault object is unchanged, and under [Late '
             'Faults](#late-faults) its fields date its report, never its condition.'),
            ('**The signed bytes survive buffering.** A reading retransmitted after a reboot '
             'carries the `v` and `liveness_nonce` it was signed with, whatever the device holds '
             'when it retransmits.'),
            ('The field costs buffer depth, in steps rather than in proportion, because a ring '
             'buffer of whole records per flash sector loses a record per sector once a record no '
             'longer fits.'),
            ("In the reference firmware's buffer the single-reading message of v1's example, with "
             'a full capability hash, is 465 bytes, and is stored as a 484-byte record, eight to '
             'a 4 KiB sector, up to 512 records in its 256 KiB ring.'),
            ('A populated `liveness_nonce` adds 52 bytes and leaves seven to a sector, up to 448 '
             'records.'),
            ('`null` adds 22 bytes and keeps eight, up to 512.'),
