            ('No contract yet defines safe-maintenance windows: their control protocol, their '
             'state machine, and when each maintenance lifecycle event is emitted.'),
            ('[ori-specs#49](https://github.com/ori-platform/ori-specs/issues/49) tracks the '
             'one that will.'),
            ('This one defines the bytes of those events.'),
        ),
        '## Required Implementation Artifacts': (
            ("In addition to v1's:"),
            ('golden vectors for **both** valid manifest shapes — one carrying '
             '`deployment_maintenance_limit_ms` and one omitting it — proving that each verifies, '
             'that the two produce different `capability_hash` values, and that duplicate, '
             'reordered, out-of-range, or non-canonical forms of the field are refused by the '
             "manifest parser's existing rules;"),
            ('a test that a device whose manifest omits the field refuses every maintenance entry;'),
            ('a runtime test that, for a device whose accepted manifest does not carry '
             '`runtime_key_domains`, it signs no command and no liveness message and reports the '
             "device's `runtime_commanded` actions unavailable when it accepts the manifest, and "
             'also when it starts over such a manifest stored before it adopted, with no '
             'republication from the device; and that for one that does, it signs both in the '
             'domains of [firmware-commands/v2.md](../firmware-commands/v2.md#signing-domains);'),
            ('a producer test that the device carries `runtime_key_domains` exactly when its '
             'verifiers verify in those domains and it accepts runtime liveness at `v` `2`;'),
            ('an interleaving test driving telemetry, fault, maintenance-event and '
             'configuration-result envelopes through **one** verifier in a single stream, proving '
             'that `seq` ordering and replay rejection hold across family boundaries and that no '
             'family has private freshness state;'),
            ("consumer tests driving the corpus through the consumer's real verification entry "
             'point, accepting every case and refusing every refusal for its declared reason;'),
            ('consumer tests driving the corpora of '
             '[ed25519-key-admission/v1](../ed25519-key-admission/v1.md) and '
             '[ed25519-verification/v1](../ed25519-verification/v1.md) through the verifier the '
             "consumer uses for this version's signatures, accepting every accepted case and "
             'refusing every refused one;'),
            ('a producer test that the device signs the `rate_limited` refusal of '
             '[firmware-commands/v2.md](../firmware-commands/v2.md) at `v` `2`, and that no fault '
             'is signed at `v` `1` once the producer implements this version;'),
            ('a producer test that each retry of a late fault carries the freshness fields of its '
             'own signing, not those of the condition or of an earlier attempt;'),
            ('a producer test, at each public boundary that builds a manifest, that it signs the '
             '`device_mode` its `channels` and `actions` determine for every combination it can '
             'declare, reproducing the mode of each accepted case of the manifest corpus from that'
             " case's arrays, and refuses to build a manifest with no channel or with any other "
             'mode;'),
            ("a producer test that, for every profile in the device's release, the bytes it hashes"
             " for `digest` are the canonical bytes of the profile's document under the grammar "
             'above, reproducing the canonical bytes and digest of each accepted document of the '
             'profile corpus from an equivalent profile;'),
            ("a producer test that the device combines an alarm word's registers in its declared "
             "word order, reproducing each interpretation case's `value` from its `registers`;"),
            ("consumer tests driving the profile corpus's range cases through the receiver's check"
             " of a bridged measurement against its channel's range;"),
            ("consumer tests driving the profile corpus's agreement cases through the receiver's "
             'check of a document against a manifest channel, using each agreeing document and '
             'refusing each disagreeing one;'),
            ('consumer tests that an alarm-word reading sharing its envelope with any other '
             "reading is accepted, is not interpreted and becomes the channel's latest reading, "
             "and that one below its channel's `quality_floor` is not refused;"),
            ('a producer test that the device signs each alarm-word reading alone in its envelope;'),
            ("consumer tests that a receiver refuses each byte string of the profile corpus's "
             '`reject_bytes`, and hashes the bytes it holds rather than a re-serialization;'),
            ('a producer test that the device signs `controller_profile` on every bridged channel '
             'and on no other, with `qualification` and `record` as its release states them;'),
            ("consumer tests driving the profile corpus through the consumer's document "
             'validation, alarm interpretation and alarm state, accepting and refusing every '
             'document as the corpus declares and reproducing every interpretation and every state'
             ' case; the state cases are stated at the longest bound, and a consumer using a '
             'shorter one expects unknown in every case whose query falls later than its bound '
             'after the last accepted reading;'),
            ("consumer tests driving the manifest corpus through the consumer's real registration "
             'path, accepting every case and refusing every refusal for its declared reason.'),
            ("consumer tests driving the envelope corpus through the consumer's real verification "
             'entry point, accepting every case and refusing every refusal for its declared '
             'reason, and converting no refused envelope into a reading;'),
            ('a producer test that a liveness message accepted after a measurement transaction '
             "begins, and before its reading is signed, is not the reading's nonce: the reading "
             'carries the nonce held when the transaction began, including when a fault owed from '
             'an earlier condition is published, or the buffer flushed, in between, and including '
             'when the liveness expiry window lapses in between;'),
            ('a producer test that an envelope including a reading whose transaction began before '
             'the held nonce was accepted, a cached reading among them, carries a nonce accepted '
             'before every one of its transactions began, or `null`;'),
            ('a producer test that a reading signed and buffered, then retransmitted after a '
             'reboot, is retransmitted with the bytes it was signed with, its `v` and '
             '`liveness_nonce` included;'),
            ('a producer test that every envelope is signed at `v` `2` with `liveness_nonce`, '
             '`null` when no nonce is held, that a heartbeat carries the nonce held when it is '
             'signed, and that no fault carries one;'),
            ('tests at the signing runtime driving the reading-age corpus through the liveness '
             'table and the age computation it uses, reproducing every query;'),
            ('tests at the signing runtime that its clock counts suspended time, that a restart '
             'empties the table, that a store restore while it runs does not, and that a reading '
             'read back from storage after a restart has no bound;'),
            ('tests at every receiver that presents firmware readings that none is presented as '
             'fresh, current or live, that only the signing runtime presents a bound, that an '
             'alarm state with a bound is presented as a snapshot polled no more than its bound '
             'ago, anchored to the instant the bound was computed, and that health and any '
             'exported snapshot or other delivered record that carries a bound names the instant '
             'it was computed, and none carries an unanchored A;'),
            ('consumer tests of the operator message, the Tier C approval request among them, '
             'driven through the path that composes it: for a firmware reading its "Measured" line'
             ' reads "not reported by device", followed, when the reading has a bound, by "polled '
             'no more than A ago, as of T" with T the runtime\'s wall-clock time when A was '
             'computed, and no message carries an A without its T; and a health report or exported'
             ' snapshot carries no A without its T.'),
            ('a producer test that a release which ships controller profiles publishes each '
             'document under the name and with the bytes [Publication](#publication) requires, '
             'once per document;'),
            ('tests at every receiver that takes profile documents from a release: it stops '
             'reading an asset at the size it derives and keeps nothing of one that reaches it; a '
             'fetching receiver builds each name from the digest it needs and holds no bytes that '
             'do not hash to it; a listing receiver drives the profile publication corpus through '
             'the function that judges a listed asset, holding each held case and refusing each '
             'refusal for its declared reason, holding nothing.'),
        ),
    },
}
# Sentences every mutation run reverses and deletes, whatever the sample.
MUTATE_ALWAYS = (
    'signs every envelope at `v` `2`',
    'retransmitted unchanged',
    'while a fault owed from an earlier condition',
    'holds no record of which',
    'Devices accept liveness at',
    'Devices sign envelopes at',
    'independently of it',
    'do not change version',
    'copy and pin it the same way',
    'MUST NOT be provisioned',
)


